# Boolean fit proofs — never printed or sliced, rendered by gate.sh.
# Each 'empty' part must render zero facets (the parts mate at their clearance);
# each 'interferes' control must render non-empty (proves the check can fail).
#
# Central screw / elevator-nut pair — single-start, so the interfering control is
# a HALF-lead (180 deg) rotation (a 90 deg control could clear and pass vacuously):
fit-mate           empty
fit-mate-ctrl      interferes
# Lid / cap-nut pair (second independent tuned thread), same 180 deg control:
lid-fit-mate       empty
lid-fit-mate-ctrl  interferes
# Knob hex torque key / screw stub — 60-deg-symmetric hex, so the control is a
# 30 deg (half-facet) rotation:
knob-fit           empty
knob-fit-ctrl      interferes
# Base-disk screw clearance — the lead-screw passes THROUGH the elevator, so its
# base disk must clear the crest. Unthreaded, so no clocking: the control is the
# old SOLID disk (no bore) that blocked the screw. Absent, this let the bug ship.
base-clear         empty
base-clear-ctrl    interferes
# Cap press fit — the top-cap bore over the screw tip (a tuned press, like the knob).
cap-fit            empty
cap-fit-ctrl       interferes
# Assembly feasibility — the elevator nut must pass the screw tip during install
# (the collar-class trap's proof in the mesh: no top feature wider than the nut
# bore). The control oversizes the tip past the nut bore so the check can fire.
tip-clear          empty
tip-clear-ctrl     interferes
